module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EtaSheafBocksteinStalk
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatIdealTorsionFree
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EtaGoodBaseChange.StalkBridge

/-!
# Feeding the ring-level goodness form of Tag 0F7X into the stalk bridge

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/EtaGoodBaseChange/StalkBridge.lean` reduces Stacks tag
0F9X, in the form `Stacks.Divisors.Eta.nonempty_derivedPullback_derivedEta_iso_of_quasiIso`
consumes it, to one quasi-isomorphism per stalk:

`𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ P^•_{f(x)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ (η_a F^•_{f(x)}) ⟶ η_b (𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ F^•_{f(x)})`.

That is verbatim the conclusion of
`Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_of_kFlat`, the ring-level
goodness form of Tag 0F7X.  This file performs the application, so that what remains of general
Tag 0F9X is exactly the list of that theorem's hypotheses read at a stalk.

Two of those hypotheses are discharged here, the regularity of the generator upstairs and of its
germ downstairs: both are `Stacks.IdealTorsion.stalkGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors`, applied on
`Y` to `ι` and on `X` to the pulled-back ideal inclusion.  The remaining ones are arguments of
the statements below; at a good triple they are supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.exists_affineOpen_stalk_goodModel`, which is how
the general form of Tag 0F9X
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.nonempty_derivedPullback_derivedEta_iso`) reaches
them.  They are:

* a bounded complex `C` of finite free `𝒪_{Y,f(x)}`-modules with `I_i(C, a)` principal and a
  quasi-isomorphism `ψ : C ⟶ F^•_{f(x)}`.  The complex and the principality are
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.exists_boundedComplex_generator_derivedStalk`;
  that produces only a *derived* isomorphism `Q(C) ≅ Q(F^•_{f(x)})`, and lifting it to a chain
  map is the companion of
  `Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.isKProjective_etaObject_toCochainComplex`;
* K-flatness of the stalk complexes of `F^•` and of `P^•`.  Stalkwise K-flatness is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.KFlatPullback.stalkCriterion`, but it is stated at the
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkComplex` spelling, over the `RingCat`-valued stalk of
  the structure sheaf; here the complex is `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.stalkComplex`, over the
  `CommRingCat`-valued one;
* flatness of the terms of the stalk complex of `F^•`.  That a flat sheaf of modules has flat
  stalks is `Stacks.IdealTorsion.stalk_flat_of_isFlat`, and it is *not* what is missing: what is
  missing is the comparison of the two `𝒪_{Y,y}`-module structures on the stalk — the
  germ-representative one `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.moduleGrpStalk`, which
  is what that lemma concludes flatness for, and the one carried by
  `(Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.stalkModuleFunctor Y y).obj M`, restriction of scalars along
  `SemilinearStalk.commStalkIso` of the module over the `RingCat`-valued stalk, which is the one
  the décalage calculus uses.  The two are not definitionally equal; the half of the comparison
  for the *structure sheaf* is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule_eq`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isRegular_stalkGenerator` and
  `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isRegular_commStalkGermMap`: a generator of the stalk ideal of an
  ideal locally generated by a nonzerodivisor is regular, upstairs and downstairs.
* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_at_stalk`: the ring-level
  goodness form of Tag 0F7X, applied at a stalk, in the spelling the stalk bridge consumes.
* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.quasiIso_comp_pullbackEtaMap_of_forall_stalk_good`: **the comparison
  of décalages at a presentation is a quasi-isomorphism** as soon as every stalk carries that
  data, with no flatness hypothesis on `f`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F9X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F9X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F7X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F7X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8S)
-/

@[expose] public section

attribute [local instance_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafedSpace.sheaf Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

open Stacks.RingedSpace (pullbackFunctor commStalkGermMap)

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace (ringStalk)

open Stacks.IdealTorsion.Reduction (stalkComplexFunctor preservesHomology_stalkModuleFunctor
  additive_stalkModuleFunctor)

universe u

namespace Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta

noncomputable section

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : X)
  (I : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf))
  (ι : I ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf)) [Mono ι]
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
  [Mono (C := SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.sheaf))
    (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)]

omit [Mono ι] [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
  [Mono (C := SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.sheaf))
    (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)] in
/-- **A generator of the stalk ideal is a nonzerodivisor**, for an ideal locally generated by a
nonzerodivisor.  This is `Stacks.IdealTorsion.stalkGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors`, read as
regularity. -/
theorem isRegular_stalkGenerator (a : ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x))
    (ha : GeneratesStalkIdeal Y ι (f.hom.base x) a)
    (hregl : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular Y ι) : IsRegular a :=
  isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mpr
    (stalkGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors Y ι hregl (f.hom.base x) a ha)

omit [Mono ι] [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf).property I]
  [Mono (C := SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.sheaf))
    (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)] in
/-- **The germ of a generator is a nonzerodivisor of `𝒪_{X,x}`** as soon as it generates the
stalk of the pulled-back ideal and that ideal is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor.  Same
proof as `Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isRegular_stalkGenerator`, applied on `X` to the inclusion
`f^*I ⟶ 𝒪_X`. -/
theorem isRegular_commStalkGermMap (a : ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x))
    (hb : GeneratesStalkIdeal X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) x (commStalkGermMap f x a))
    (hregl : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)) :
    IsRegular (commStalkGermMap f x a) :=
  isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mpr
    (stalkGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) hregl x
      (commStalkGermMap f x a) hb)

variable
  (F : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf)) ℤ)
  (hF : ∀ n : ℤ, IsIdealTorsionFree Y ι (F.X n))
  (a : ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ha : GeneratesStalkIdeal Y ι (f.hom.base x) a)
  (hb : GeneratesStalkIdeal X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) x (commStalkGermMap f x a))

omit [Mono (C := SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.sheaf))
    (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι)] in
include ha hb in
/-- **The ring-level goodness form of Tag 0F7X, applied at a stalk.**  Let `ι : I ⟶ 𝒪_Y` be
locally generated by a nonzerodivisor and let `f^*I ⟶ 𝒪_X` be too; let `a` generate `I_{f(x)}`
and let its germ `b` generate `(f^*I)_x`.  Suppose the stalk complex of `F^•` at `f x` is K-flat
with flat terms and receives a quasi-isomorphism from a bounded complex `C` of finite free
`𝒪_{Y,f(x)}`-modules whose determinantal ideals `I_i(C, a)` are principal, and let
`p : P^• ⟶ η_I F^•` be a quasi-isomorphism whose stalk complex at `f x` is K-flat.  Then

`𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ P^•_{f(x)} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ (η_a F^•_{f(x)}) ⟶ η_b (𝒪_{X,x} ⊗ F^•_{f(x)})`

is a quasi-isomorphism — which is exactly the stalkwise hypothesis of
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.quasiIso_comp_pullbackEtaMap_of_forall_stalk`.

This is `Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_of_kFlat` at
`A = 𝒪_{Y,f(x)}`, `B = 𝒪_{X,x}`, `𝒦 = F^•_{f(x)}` and `P = P^•_{f(x)}`, with the regularity
hypotheses discharged by
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isRegular_stalkGenerator` and
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.isRegular_commStalkGermMap`, and the quasi-isomorphism out of
`P^•_{f(x)}` obtained from `p` by exactness of the stalk functor followed by the comparison of
Tag 0GT6.  **No flatness of `f` is used.** -/
theorem quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_at_stalk
    (hreglY : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular Y ι)
    (hreglX : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι))
    (C : BoundedComplex (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)))
    (hI : ∀ i : ℤ, (idealI C a i).IsPrincipal)
    (hKF : CochainComplex.KFlat.{u, u} (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) F))
    (hflat : ∀ i : ℤ,
      Module.Flat (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) ((stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) F).X i))
    (ψ : C.toCochainComplex ⟶ stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) F) (hψ : QuasiIso ψ)
    (P : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf)) ℤ)
    (hKP : CochainComplex.KFlat.{u, u} (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) P))
    (p : P ⟶ etaObj Y I ι F hF) (hp : QuasiIso p) :
    letI : Algebra (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ringStalk X x) :=
      (commStalkGermMap f x).toAlgebra
    QuasiIso (Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.baseChangeMap (B := ringStalk X x)
          ((stalkComplexFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)).map p ≫
            (etaStalkIso Y I ι F hF (f.hom.base x) a ha).hom) ≫
        Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.etaBaseChangeMap (B := ringStalk X x) a
          (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) F)) := by
  let : Algebra (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base x)) (ringStalk X x) := (commStalkGermMap f x).toAlgebra
  have := preservesHomology_stalkModuleFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)
  -- the stalk functor's additivity is stated as a theorem and supplied explicitly, like its
  -- `PreservesZeroMorphisms`, because the category in the middle of the composite carries two
  -- spellings of the same `RingCat` stalk
  have := additive_stalkModuleFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)
  have hps : QuasiIso ((stalkComplexFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)).map p ≫
      (etaStalkIso Y I ι F hF (f.hom.base x) a ha).hom) :=
    (quasiIso_iff_of_arrow_mk_iso ((stalkComplexFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)).map p) _
      (Arrow.isoMk' _ _ (Iso.refl _) (etaStalkIso Y I ι F hF (f.hom.base x) a ha)
        (Category.id_comp _))).1
      (HomologicalComplex.quasiIso_map_of_preservesHomology p (stalkModuleFunctor Y (f.hom.base x)))
  exact Stacks.Eta.GoodBaseChange.quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_of_kFlat
    C a (isRegular_stalkGenerator f x I ι a ha hreglY)
    (isRegular_commStalkGermMap f x I ι a hb hreglX) hI
    (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) F) hKF hflat ψ hψ
    (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base x) P) hKP _ hps

include hF in
/-- **The comparison of décalages at a presentation is a quasi-isomorphism when every stalk
carries a good finite free model**, with no flatness hypothesis on `f`.

At every point `z` of `X` the data asked for is: a generator `a` of `I_{f(z)}` whose germ
generates `(f^*I)_z`, a bounded complex `C` of finite free `𝒪_{Y,f(z)}`-modules with all
determinantal ideals `I_i(C, a)` principal and a quasi-isomorphism `C ⟶ F^•_{f(z)}`, and
K-flatness of the stalk complexes of `F^•` and `P^•` together with flatness of the terms of the
former.  That is exactly the ring-level goodness hypothesis of Stacks tag 0F7X at that stalk.

The two steps are
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_at_stalk`, which turns
that data into the stalkwise quasi-isomorphism, and
`Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta.quasiIso_comp_pullbackEtaMap_of_forall_stalk`, which is the stalk
bridge. -/
theorem quasiIso_comp_pullbackEtaMap_of_forall_stalk_good
    (hF' : ∀ n : ℤ, IsIdealTorsionFree X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) ((pullbackComplex f F).X n))
    (hreglY : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular Y ι)
    (hreglX : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι))
    (P : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.sheaf)) ℤ)
    (p : P ⟶ etaObj Y I ι F hF) (hp : QuasiIso p)
    (hgood : ∀ z : X, ∃ (a : ringStalk Y (f.hom.base z)),
        GeneratesStalkIdeal Y ι (f.hom.base z) a ∧
        GeneratesStalkIdeal X (pullbackIdealIncl f I ι) z (commStalkGermMap f z a) ∧
        ∃ (C : BoundedComplex (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base z)))
        (ψ : C.toCochainComplex ⟶ stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base z) F),
        (∀ i : ℤ, (idealI C a i).IsPrincipal) ∧ QuasiIso ψ ∧
          CochainComplex.KFlat.{u, u} (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base z) F) ∧
          (∀ i : ℤ, Module.Flat (ringStalk Y (f.hom.base z))
            ((stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base z) F).X i)) ∧
          CochainComplex.KFlat.{u, u} (stalkComplex Y (f.hom.base z) P)) :
    QuasiIso (((pullbackFunctor f).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).map p ≫
      pullbackEtaMap f I ι F hF hF') := by
  refine quasiIso_comp_pullbackEtaMap_of_forall_stalk f I ι F hF hF' P p fun z => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hb, C, ψ, hI, hψ, hKF, hflat, hKP⟩ := hgood z
  exact ⟨a, ha, hb, quasiIso_baseChangeMap_comp_etaBaseChangeMap_at_stalk f z I ι F hF a ha hb
    hreglY hreglX C hI hKF hflat ψ hψ P hKP p hp⟩

end

end Stacks.IdealTorsion.Eta

end
